NV shared operation packet fixtures
===================================

The reference driver executes NVComputeQueue/NVCopyQueue, nv_build_program and
QMD from tinygrad a83c6f8011863c17ef4e9c24c59e521be3c754d3. Device construction
and submission are bypassed; packet generation and program parsing are not.
The OCaml driver executes Encoded_queue.encode and inspects its typed
initialization stores at the same fixed addresses. Neither driver opens a GPU.
These are encoding checks, not evidence of hardware execution.

Reproduce from the repository root, using an extracted reference checkout:
  python3 packages/tolk/test/golden/nvqueue/generate_expected.py \
    --tinygrad _plans/tinygrad-a83c6f801 --output _plans/goldens-a83/nvqueue

Output is mandatory and no expected/actual files are read. Review the independent
output before replacing expectations. Format: one lowercase eight-digit dword
per line, little-endian byte interpretation, trailing newline.

The 40 cases cover setup, local-memory setup, barriers, waits, releases,
timestamps, copy chunking, program descriptors and chained execution on Ada
and Blackwell. Program metadata comes from the committed simple_add_sm89.cubin
fixture rather than a copied NVProgram template. Using that binary to inspect a
Blackwell descriptor does not assert that the sm89 code executes on Blackwell.
Image/QMD/signal addresses are 0x100000/0x300000/0x400000. The three arguments
are 0x900000/0xa00000/0xb00000 and scalar n=32. Launch dimensions are (4,3,2)
and (8,4,1). The second QMD follows the target's descriptor/argument stride.

The OCaml encoder appends its documented command-storage progress release to
every submission. The fixture verifies that trailer's size, opcode and flags,
then compares the operation payload before it. Runtime tests separately check
progress values, publication, retained storage and replay. Descriptor bytes are
compared without masking fields.

Migration attribution
---------------------
Original fixtures came from baa6148066 (Raven 296a37964); eight releases were
subsequently regenerated from 471a3aeb (Raven 27ccb18f2). Upstream c84876fdd
moved NV to HCQ2, separating signal/timestamp release semantics and moving QMDs
before arguments in shared per-submission storage. This driver now invokes that
actual path with the committed ELF, so descriptor resource fields and program
entry/constant-buffer offsets intentionally replace the old synthetic metadata.
The 16 exec/QMD files change for that reason; the other 24 payloads are stable.

Retired write32/write64/poll_bit_set/poll_bit_clear cases (two chips each) have
no counterpart in the target queue API or surviving production callers. They
are removed, not reconstructed in the reference driver. Raw setup packets are
still inputs used by NVDevice setup/SLM growth, encoded through shared INS(nv).
